+# Cancelling a Booked Visit Stays Out of Scope
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+This ADR amends NG-5 as recorded in [Deleting Records and Amending Booked Visits Are Deliberately Out of Scope](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md).
+
+NG-5 declined both changing and cancelling a visit once booked, and the 2026-08-08 non-goal ADR confirmed that row as deliberate. That ADR requires a later narrowing to be a recorded owner decision with its own non-goal ADR.
+
+A feature request on 2026-09-30 asks for correcting a booked visit. The owner decided NG-5 at intake, quoted verbatim:
+
+> Non-goal NG-5 is narrowed: cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope, but correcting its date and description is now in. Record the narrowing the way the project records non-goal changes.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-5 whole.** Not chosen: the owner put correction of a booked visit in scope.
+2. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation** (chosen, by the owner's decision above).
+3. **Retire NG-5.** Not chosen: the owner kept cancellation out of scope.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-5 now declines only cancelling a visit once booked. Correcting a booked visit's date and description is in scope, as `REQ-VIS-003`. The owner's decision above is the whole authority for the change; this ADR adds no reason of its own.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A booked visit is no longer immutable: its date and description can be corrected.
+- A booked visit still cannot be cancelled, and NG-4 still declines deleting a visit.
+- A correction is held to the booking rules. A past visit can be corrected only by moving its date past today — an open question in the PRD.
+- No page links to the correction yet; a visible way in may come as a follow-up request.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-5 row.
+- [PRD Visits](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — the correction requirement the narrowing admits.
